 # Setup pstack
 
-Write `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`, an always-applied rule that sets pstack's model per role.
+Save accepted choices in `$CODEX_HOME/pstack-codex/models.json`, or `~/.codex/pstack-codex/models.json` when `CODEX_HOME` is unset. Resolve helpers relative to this installed skill and invoke their absolute paths with Node.js. Read [the helper contract](references/models-contract.md) for shapes and arguments.
 
-## Steps
+For removal, run `scripts/register-agents.mjs --unregister` while this bundle is available, then remove the plugin. Unregister removes only unchanged owned registrations and retains preferences. A fresh reset removes the old installation through its own setup before installing this product. There is no old-name alias or automatic preference migration.
 
-### 1. Detect available models
+## 1. Choose worker executors
 
-Enumerate the model slugs you can pass to a `Task` subagent in this session. That is the dependable source. If Cursor also exposes a models API or CLI that lists the user's entitled models, prefer it for completeness. If you cannot detect any, ask the user to paste the slugs they have access to. Never write a real slug you have not confirmed is available. The aliases `inherit-parent` and `auto` are always valid even though they are not detected slugs.
+Start by asking which worker executors to use, unless the conversation already supplies the choice. Offer the available worker executors independently. Native Codex, Claude Code, and Antigravity can be selected in any combination. The parent chat stays in Codex. Prefill the executors used by saved choices on a rerun. Do not infer a worker model from the chosen executors.
 
-### 2. Load current state
+Only selected executors need installation and login checks. Unselected worker CLIs are neither invoked nor required. If a previously saved entry uses an executor the user now excludes, show that entry and obtain its replacement before saving. Preserve every other accepted choice.
 
-The default role-to-model mapping is the rule shape shown in step 5 below. If `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc` already exists, read it and treat its `# budget` line and its role values as the current choices. Otherwise start from those defaults. A line whose role is not in step 5, such as `how explorer` or `why investigators`, is from a retired role. Drop it.
+## 2. Prepare the selected CLIs
 
-A rule without the `# defaults: 2` line comes from an older setup. That setup wrote a line for every role, so some of its values are old defaults, not choices. An old slug is one that matches `grok-*`. Before step 3, replace these values:
+Check `node --version`. Helpers require Node.js 24.12 or newer. Codex registration also needs Python 3.11 or newer. Use [CLI installation and login](references/cli-prerequisites.md) when a prerequisite is missing.
 
-- An old slug in `feature, refactoring`, `bug-fix`, `perf-issue`, `hillclimb`, `reflect tooling`, or `swarm workers` takes the role's step 5 default.
-- A `claude-opus-*` value in `hardest tasks` takes the role's step 5 default.
-- In a panel role (`arena runners`, `arena cross-judge pool`, `architect runners`, `interrogate reviewers`), a list of exactly one `claude-opus-*` entry and one old slug, in either order, takes the role's step 5 list. In any other list, each old slug becomes `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast`.
+For selected Claude Code workers, run the sibling `poteto-mode/scripts/run-claude.mjs detect`. Report its executable, version, compatibility, safe auth status, and guidance. If missing, guide the authorized CLI installation. If logged out, guide human login in the user's terminal. Rerun detection afterward. Reuse existing authentication and configuration. Never copy credentials into a test home or setup file. Detection does not install tools, authenticate, or prove model access. If login status cannot be established, inspect the selected CLI's normal status flow with the user before choosing its models.
 
-Every other value is the user's choice and stays, including an old slug in any other role and every `inherit-parent` or `auto` value. Tell the user which values you replaced.
+For selected Antigravity workers, run the sibling `poteto-mode/scripts/run-agy.mjs detect`. Use the prerequisite guide for the official agy CLI. Let the user choose subscription login, Gemini API key, or ADC, and prepare that method with the guide. Reuse a method the user keeps. Never read credentials, ask the user to paste a key into the conversation, or switch methods silently. Rerun detection and confirm its `auth.method` before collecting the source-labeled catalog below. The catalog reflects the active method. Detection proves required syntax and version and reports the inherited method. It does not prove authentication or model access.
 
-### 3. Budget, map, and confirm
+The [execution binding](../poteto-mode/references/execution.md) describes runtime capability checks. A global CLI effort list proves syntax only. It supplies no default model or account entitlement.
 
-**(a) Ask for a budget.** Prefer AskQuestion over free text. Offer these four options with these exact labels, and name the current budget when the rule records one. With no rule, say that `large` matches the skill defaults.
+## 3. Load choices and collect supported models
 
-- `unlimited — max reasoning`
-- `large — xhigh reasoning`
-- `medium — high reasoning`
-- `small — medium reasoning`
+Run `scripts/models.mjs read` and retain `config`, `proposal`, `needsChoice`, `droppedRoles`, and `sha256`. Fresh `config.roles` is empty. The proposal presents all 13 roles with unresolved model slots. Scalars start with one slot and panels or pools with three. Saved choices prefill the proposal and remain authoritative. Missing roles execute on the actual native parent with their original counts, disclosed as `unconfigured`. Setup is optional before a task.
 
-**(b) Apply it.** Build the working table from the skill defaults, and on a re-run keep any role you changed by family, list, or alias (`inherit-parent`, `auto`). Families are the ones Phase A of the **arena** skill defines, so Fable is its own family. Each role has a target effort, which is its default's effort moved by the budget. `large` keeps it, `unlimited` raises it one step, `medium` lowers it one step, and `small` lowers it two steps, on the ladder `max` > `xhigh` > `high` > `medium` > `low`. A target at either end of the ladder stays there. Most defaults are at `xhigh`, and each budget label names where those land. Set the effort token of every real slug in the role, panel entries included, to the role's target. The effort token is the last token, or the one before a trailing `fast`. If the result is not a detected slug, use the same family's detected slug with the highest effort at or below the target, else mark the role as needing a choice. `inherit-parent` and `auto` do not change. So `unlimited` turns `claude-opus-5-5-xhigh` into `claude-opus-5-5-max` and `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast` into `claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-fast`, and it keeps `claude-fable-5-2-max`. Gemini tops out at `high`, so under `unlimited` the fallback keeps `gemini-4-carbon-high` as it is. `small` turns the first two into `claude-opus-5-5-medium` and `claude-opus-5-5-low-fast`. Fable 5.2 and Gemini have no fast slug, so never write one.
+A retired role in the saved file, such as `how explorer` or `why investigators`, appears in `droppedRoles` and not in `config`. Show each one to the user. The next save drops it. Any other unknown role still fails validation.
 
-**(c) Show the roles and confirm.** Show every role with its model, marking any real slug not in the detected set as needing a choice. Also list each line step 2 dropped. Ask whether to accept as-is or change specific roles, offering the detected models plus `inherit-parent` and `auto` (both mean: this role runs on the parent chat model, which is how Auto users stay on Auto) as the options. Prefer AskQuestion over free text. For panel roles (arena runners, architect runners, interrogate reviewers) the value is a list, and one subagent runs per entry, alias entries included, so the list length sets the count. `arena cross-judge pool` is also a list, but Arena runs one judge. It tries only values from a vendor other than the parent's, in list order, so order it by preference. Fable and the other Claude models are one vendor. An `inherit-parent` or `auto` value never judges. `swarm workers` is the default model for every worker unless a race or comparison assigns another model per arm.
+For selected native Codex workers, enumerate exact model IDs and supported efforts from this session's native tools or Codex `model/list`. Collect every page. For selected Claude workers, collect model-specific host or configuration evidence, or ask for confirmation of the exact model and its efforts. Label that source. A configured candidate alone does not prove access. Honor confirmation already supplied in the conversation.
 
-### 4. Validate
+For selected Antigravity workers, run the sibling `poteto-mode/scripts/run-agy.mjs catalog --cwd ABSOLUTE_PROJECT --run-dir ABSOLUTE_NEW_LOCAL_DIRECTORY`. Pass its sanitized `catalog.json` through `--agy-catalog ABSOLUTE_AGY_CATALOG` when normalizing. No model prompt is submitted. Fixed-effort labels establish only the reported variant's configured availability. Unclassified candidates need per-model evidence before selection.
 
-Every real slug written must be in the detected set. `inherit-parent` and `auto` always pass. If a chosen real slug is not available, stop and ask again.
+Normalize the combined catalog with `scripts/models.mjs catalog --input ABSOLUTE_JSON`. Include `--claude-runtime ABSOLUTE_DETECT_JSON` only when configuring external Claude entries. Every Claude entry needs its own source and efforts expressible by that runtime. See [model capability records](references/models-contract.md#model-capability-records). No fixed Sol, Opus, or other model is required.
 
-### 5. Write the rule
+For Antigravity-only worker choices, skip native and Claude probes and model collection. Normalize with `scripts/models.mjs catalog --agy-catalog ABSOLUTE_AGY_CATALOG` alone. For any combination, include only the selected catalogs.
 
-Write `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc` with `alwaysApply: true`, the `# defaults: 2` line, a `# budget` line with the chosen label and the effort that label names, and one line per role, using the same labels poteto-mode uses. Overwrite the whole file so re-runs stay idempotent. Shape:
+`auto` and `inherit-parent` always mean the actual native Codex parent. They omit a separate effort and cannot select an external executor. Bind them through Codex execution's parent-selection rules.
 
